      "result": {
        "reply_text": "You can bring a product liability action against a product manufacturer, service provider, or product seller for any harm caused by a defective product under Section 83 of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019. Furthermore, under Section 39 of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, if the District Commission is satisfied that the goods suffer from a defect, it can order the opposite party to return the price paid along with such interest as may be decided, or to replace the goods with new goods of similar description free from any defect. To seek a resolution, you can approach the National Consumer Helpline online at https://consumerhelpline.gov.in/ or call their Toll-Free Numbers: 1915 or 1800-11-4000.\n\nKeep your purchase receipt, warranty card, photographs or videos of the broken toaster, and records of any communication with the seller ready as proof.\n\n1. Lodge a grievance with the National Consumer Helpline online or via phone.\n2. If the issue is not resolved, you may approach the District Commission where the value of goods or services does not exceed the prescribed limit and where the cause of action arises or the opposite party carries on business.\n\nA product manufacturer is liable in a product liability action if the product contains a manufacturing defect, is defective in design, deviates from manufacturing specifications, does not conform to the express warranty, or fails to contain adequate instructions or warnings, as outlined in Section 84 of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019.\n\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 83\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 39\nSource: Department of Consumer Affairs - National Consumer Helpline (NCH), H NCH\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 84\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
